# Stop full-layer repaints that nothing asked for, plus the paint log that found
# them.
# Merged from: webkit-no-full-repaint-on-layer-grow,
# webkit-no-full-repaint-on-composited-move, webkit-paint-log-diagnostic.
#
#  - LAYER GROWTH: a layer changing size does not need a whole repaint — the
#    coordinated tiled backing store keeps existing tile content valid across
#    resizes and only newly exposed tiles need painting. During a heavy load the
#    page content layer grows every time an image/ad lands, and each growth
#    full-repainted the page (device-proven on franceinfo.fr: 572 whole-layer
#    invalidations, ~595 Mpx = 219 screenfuls CPU-rastered in ONE load). Covers
#    the generic GraphicsLayer::setSize() path
#    (shouldRepaintOnSizeChange override) and the explicit scrolled-contents
#    resize invalidation in RenderLayerBacking::updateGeometry() (grow-only skip;
#    shrink and padding-box offset changes still repaint).
#    WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_LAYER_RESIZE=1 = stock.
#  - COMPOSITED MOVE: the scroll-time analog. A self-painting composited layer
#    that merely MOVED (or jittered <= 1px in size) during a layout does not need
#    its whole backing re-rastered. franceinfo.fr runs a full doc layout on ~every
#    scroll frame, and recursiveUpdateLayerPositions -> repaintAfterLayoutIfNeeded
#    then full-repainted each of ~14 composited section layers whose location
#    shifted (device-proven build 524: 11x onche.org's full-layer paint = the felt
#    ~10x scroll slowdown). Only skips move/jitter of layers that own their
#    backing store; forced/style repaints and ancestor-painting layers unaffected.
#    WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_COMPOSITED_MOVE=1 = stock.
#  - WEBKIT_PAINT_LOG=1 (WebProcess stderr, zero overhead when unset) logs
#    per-layer damage (GLC FULL/RECT), per-proxy dirty rects (INVAL), tile-paint
#    passes (PAINT) and full tile drops (DROP-ALL with reason). This is the tool
#    that root-caused both of the above and the franceinfo repaint storm; kept
#    because that class of bug recurs on every site.
#
# NOTE: the load-rendering-throttle patches that once sat here are GONE (dropped
# after builds 465-471) and must not be retried. Coalescing main-thread rendering
# updates during load fundamentally deadlocks the compositor's
# composition <- tiles <- flush handshake: moving during a load reveals content
# whose tiles are painted by updateRendering(), and deferring that paint sticks
# m_isWaitingForRenderer true = permanent freeze (reproduced every attempt, incl.
# the observer+timer and compositor-gated variants). It also never moved DCL
# (raster is on Skia worker threads). If load-time paint work is revisited, target
# style-recalc/layout coalescing, off the compositor path.
# See docs/investigations/ and memory franceinfo-load-slowness-analysis.
#
# ---
